<p>16. <strong>What is the difference between synchronous and asynchronous code?</strong></p>
<p>Answer: Synchronous code executes line by line, blocking the next operation until the current one completes. Asynchronous code allows multiple operations to run concurrently, with callbacks, promises, or async/await handling the results.</p>
